From dfb01b6db96e6cdab7edbe264c26a1fe3ca74014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 18:47:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf phase 11 patch 0136 -- wave-42 all-notes-off fix on
 real DreamBlaster S2

Wave-41 real-HW operator finding: music note hangs indefinitely after
engine quit on g2k Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster S2; persists until
machine reboot. Affects PLAY3/PLAY4 in the wave-41-valid iter where
DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND=wb is engaged.

Root cause (flush-instr WAVE-41-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec. 4.2): the existing
on_song_stop / dtor all-notes-off path was running (per captured log
lines "wb backend: on_song_stop" + "wb backend shutdown (MPU-401 reset
issued)") but the silence dispatch was failing to reach the DreamBlaster
S2 daughterboard. SDL/0047's claim that DSP cmd 0xD3 (audio backend
CloseDevice's speaker-off) silences MIDI output alongside DAC was
empirically refuted: the WaveBlaster header is MIDI-bus driven, NOT
DAC-driven, so 0xD3 doesn't reach it.

flush-instr's three failure-mode hypotheses (all engine-domain except
(c)):
  (a) WB backend dtor logic bug under DSP cmd 0x38 dispatch
      (some subtle state interaction with concurrent SDL audio DSP DMA
      programming during teardown)
  (b) MidiScheduler::stop not always firing on_song_stop at shutdown
      (only at song-change)
  (c) DreamBlaster S2 firmware quirk ignoring CC 123 in some mode
      (rare; not engine-fixable)

Mitigation: add an EARLIER explicit emit at the engine-shutdown
boundary, well before the SDL audio backend's DSP DMA stops (the most
plausible trigger for (a)/(b)). The existing on_song_stop + dtor
all-notes-off path stays in place as belt-and-suspenders; this is
ADDITIONAL coverage, not a replacement.

API surface added:

  MidiBackend::silence_for_shutdown()  -- new virtual, default no-op.
    Called by MidiScheduler::silence_for_shutdown() BEFORE
    SoundManager teardown touches the DSP. Backend has free rein to
    emit chip-specific silence commands.

  MidiBackendWaveBlaster::silence_for_shutdown()  -- override; emits
    CC 123 (All Notes Off) on each of 16 MIDI channels via the
    DSP-mediated path (SDL_DOSMpu401WriteByte -> DSP cmd 0x38).
    Tighter than the existing _all_notes_off_all_channels: emits ONLY
    CC 123 (graceful release), not both CC 120 + CC 123. Reduces total
    byte count from 96 to 48; lower interleave risk with concurrent
    SDL audio teardown. Per flush-instr's specific recommendation at
    LOG-ANALYSIS sec. 4.2 final paragraph.

  MidiScheduler::silence_for_shutdown()  -- new public method; thin
    wrapper that calls _backend->silence_for_shutdown() if a backend
    is bound. Does NOT mutate _playing or release the backend. Safe
    to call any number of times.

  SoundManager::shutdown()  -- new snd-shutdown[0/6] step invokes
    MidiScheduler::silence_for_shutdown() BEFORE the existing
    snd-shutdown[1/6] (MidiScheduler::shutdown). doskutsu_dbg_log
    bracket logged via SDL/0024's per-line fsync to PAUSESDL.LOG.

Stub + OPL3 backends inherit the default no-op silence_for_shutdown()
from the base class -- their existing on_song_stop / dtor paths are
correctness-complete (Stub has nothing to silence; OPL3's dtor
unconditional 18-voice KEY-OFF works because OPL3 is a direct-register
write path with no DSP cmd indirection that could fail).

Single-mechanism preservation per
[[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]: this is a
correctness patch on the wave-41-valid-TAS binary (sha 466976316b9d).
Default-OFF behavior bit-identical: silence_for_shutdown only fires
when a backend with a non-default override is bound (= when WB
backend is engaged via DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND=wb). PLAY1 (no audio
backend env var) sees the no-op base implementation; wave-41 fps
anchor comparison preserved.

DOSBox-X smoke gate: no DreamBlaster S2 emulation per
WAVE-41-DOSBOX-PROFILING-PLAN sec. 5.1, so DOSBox-X cannot validate
the actual silence behavior. Smoke verifies:
  - Binary builds clean
  - String 'wb backend: silence_for_shutdown' present in .rodata
  - snd-shutdown[0/6] banner fires at shutdown in RECORDSD.LOG
  - make tas-smoke PASS (no regression on default organya backend)
Real-HW verification gates on operator's ear in wave-42-valid PLAY4
(quit-cycle ear-test cell per WAVE-41-LOG-ANALYSIS sec. 5.3).

Coordination: peer-DM build-qa with new sha for re-gate + new banner
regex; peer-DM realhw with new sha for wave-42 tarball composition.

